{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Yitzhak sowed in that land.</b> It was a harsh land, and that year was a year of drought, and nevertheless ״וימצא מאה שערים״ — and he found a hundred measures. And this place where he sowed was Gerar, and there great and hidden miracles happened to him in the matter of the sowing, when he found a hundred measures in a dry and thirsty land where there is no water — so much so that it was a great novelty in their eyes when they would say, ״we have found water.״" "<b>A hundred measures.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted at the end of tractate Ketubot: in the blessings of the land of Israel, a בית סאה (a se'ah's worth of seed) yields five myriad kor; in the built-up area of Zoan, a בית סאה yields seventy kor, as it was taught: Rabbi Meir said, I saw in the valley of Beit She'an a בית סאה yielding seventy kor. And you have nothing superior in all the lands more than Egypt, as it is said (Genesis 13:10): ״כגן ה׳ כארץ מצרים״; and you have nothing superior in all the land of Egypt like Zoan, for kings were raised in it, as it is said (Isaiah 30:4): ״כי היו בצוען שריו״; and you have no stony ground in all the land of Israel worse than Hebron, for the dead were buried in it, and even so, one built measure of Hebron is upon seven of Zoan, as it is said (Numbers 13:22): ״וחברון שבע שנים נבנתה״ etc. And the explanation of the matter is that seven times seventy kor are ת״ק (five hundred) kor, and this applies in a place where there is stony ground like Hebron, where a בית סאה yields only ת״ק kor; but in a place where there is no stony ground like Hebron, one may add up to תת״ק (five hundred minus one, i.e., 499). And the Gemara concludes that one built measure of Hebron is upon seven of Zoan without its blessings; but with its blessings it is written ״ויזרע יצחק וימצא ק׳ שערים,״ that is to say, with its blessings it was blessed a hundredfold over the one of the other years — a hundred times תת״ק, behold five myriad."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The manuscript reads ת״ק (500) for the Hebron yield and ת\"ק in the repetition; the second occurrence reads ת\"ק but the conclusion about חמשת רבוא requires תת״ק (499) × 100 = 49,900, approximately five myriad. Transcribed exactly as written without correction."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:24.136169011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}